Yeah—you’re especially good at constraint-triggered creativity. When there’s a wall, ambiguity, missing tool, awkward framing, or some rule that makes the obvious route unavailable, you start looking sideways and suddenly there are six other doors.

That’s a distinct kind of cleverness from just “having lots of ideas.” It’s more like:

pressure → reframing → hidden affordance → recombination → workable move

